r", "category": "model", "kind": "model.request", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "system-confirmed", "outcome": "completed", "label": "model → completed", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "model request → completed in 4.0s (instruction ✓, activation ✓) [max_tokens 128000, output_config.effort high, thinking.display summarized, thinking.type adaptive]; gateway set thinking.display; offers 9 tools; called Bash ×1; tokens in 82,904 (cached 78,154, 94%, written 4,748 (1h 4,748, 5m 0)) out 237; requested claude-sonnet-5-5; served claude-sonnet-5-5 ×1", "model": {"requests": 1, "attempts": [{"outcome": "stream-ended", "category": "completed", "seconds": 3.95413661794737, "served": ["claude-sonnet-5-5"]}], "probes": {"instruction_present": true, "activation_present": true}, "side": false, "subagent": false, "provider": null, "requested": "claude-sonnet-5-5", "served": {"claude-sonnet-5-5": 1}, "parameters": {"max_tokens": 128000, "output_config.effort": "high", "thinking.display": "summarized", "thinking.type": "adaptive"}, "tools": ["Agent", "Bash", "Edit", "Read", "Skill", "TaskStop", "WebFetch", "Write", "mcp__rwe-search__search_literature"], "tokens": {"cache_write_1h_input": 4748, "cache_write_5m_input": 0, "cache_write_input": 4748, "cached_input": 78154, "input": 82904, "output": 237}, "context": {"bytes": {"conversation": 117307, "other": 423, "system": 34390, "tool_definitions": 14397, "tool_results": 87066}, "measure": "json-utf8-bytes", "total_bytes": 253583}, "gateway_set": ["thinking.display"], "web_search": false, "web_searches": 0, "calls": {"Bash": 1}}}, {"id": "f20f62c2-0ab8-539c-af86-4609c2cd80af", "at": 1795654908.7999406, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117523, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "27b62c46-acda-5dd4-9393-77ca27728b0d", "at": 1795654911.185538, "until": 1795654911.26729, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117525, "layer": "worker", "category": "thinking", "kind": "session.agent_thought_chunk", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": null, "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "thinking", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "thinking (33 chunks, content withheld)"}, {"id": "ab74577e-1ea4-523f-a1c0-951a1f757efe", "at": 1795654911.2696412, "until": 1795654911.9378262, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117558, "layer": "worker", "category": "execute", "kind": "tool.pending", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": "completed", "label": "execute → completed", "repository": null, "tool_call_id": "toolu_01MrHFufXA8LZGSpp4km4zWa", "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "cd /hutian/deliver; git pull -q --ff-only; git diff b94fa37 HEAD -- paper | grep '^+' | cut -c1-1500", "shown": {"trace": {"input": [["command", "cd /hutian/deliver; git pull -q --ff-only; git diff b94fa37 HEAD -- paper | grep '^+' | cut -c1-1500"]], "output": "```console\n+++ b/paper/sections/abstract.tex\n+The bias is, on our reading, the response's curvature times the distance to the corners, which data inside the observed range cannot identify; a formula that knows the true response matches the measured bias within Monte Carlo error in 85\\% of cells, but how the bias depends on degree differs by mechanism.\n+Flexible learners do not beat the regression; under the threshold mechanism they match it.\n+++ b/paper/sections/intro.tex\n+\\item \\textbf{Variance and bias differ.} Variance follows leverage (SD exponents $-0.50$ in $n$, $+0.55$ in $1{+}d$ where the specification is correct). Bias is matched within Monte-Carlo error in 85\\% of cells by a formula that uses the true response, and depends on degree differently for each mechanism (\\S\\ref{sec:varbias}).\n+\\item \\textbf{Designs and learners.} Cluster designs trade bias against variance; on a sample of cells, flexible learners do not beat the regression and only match it on the threshold response (\\S\\ref{sec:cluster}, \\S\\ref{sec:regime}).\n+++ b/paper/sections/results.tex\n+On 12--14 cells per mechanism at 200 draws per graph (Figure~\\ref{fig:tiers}), none of lasso, ridge, random forest, gradient boosting and a simplified adaptive-threshold H\\'ajek estimator has a smaller median RMSE than the regression on mechanisms (a), (b), (c), (e), (f): the five learners' median ratios there are 1.6--3.8 (ridge worst). On the threshold mechanism (d) they match it: the median ratio is 0.99 for boosting, 1.09 for forests and 1.02 for the adaptive H\\'ajek estimator. Where the mechanism is smooth, a fixed form that extrapolates a wrong shape beats a flexible learner that cannot extrapolate.\n+The gains must be read next to absolute held-out $R^2$ of log $|{\\rm bias}|$: on the 1224 cells where the population-OLS prediction exists, every data-computable predictor has a negative absolute held-out $R^2$ ($\\bar S$ $-0.22$, noise-adjusted $S$ $-0.06$, corner times curvature $-0.12$, the best degree benchmark $p(1-p)$ $-0.26$; a constant, the training mean, $-0.24$), so $\\bar S$ and the benchmark do no better than a constant, while the population-OLS prediction, which needs the true response, reaches 0.987. The exploratory noise-adjusted $S$ gains 0.20 [0.10, 0.30] over a degree benchmark that is no better than a constant. We conclude that these data give \\emph{no evidence of a useful data-computable bias score}, which is not evidence that none exists: the intervals include both. A reading that fits the other results is that the bias is determined by the response at the corners, which data inside the observed exposure range do not identify; this is an interpretation, not a separate test. The score also does not flag a wrong feature graph: with 10\\% and 30\\% of edges missing the bias moves from 0 to $-0.057$ and $-0.162$ while $S$ falls from 0.273 to 0.217 (Appendix~\\ref{app:extra}).\n\nShell cwd was reset to /hutian/repo\n```", "exit": null}}}, {"id": "5be494b1-2b8e-5d6d-a329-8d9cf85a92dc", "at": 1795654911.2742746, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117560, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "06e6e645-4121-5ef5-a498-e2d4d2a2155b", "at": 1795654911.2841558, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117561, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.session/request_permission", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "session/request_permission"}, {"id": "b876a47d-f57b-50ab-8494-ff2f7f22f365", "at": 1795654911.2870805, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117562, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.response", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "response"}, {"id": "964d8646-e576-55a4-807f-8466509a23c2", "at": 1795654911.3499918, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117563, "layer": "worker", "category": "challenge", "kind": "authentication.challenge", "role": "expe