": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.agent_message_chunk", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "message", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "message (65 chunks)", "shown": {"message": "I read `paper-repo` `dev` at `b157b0d`, which adds the constant row to the text, and posted two wording corrections in `experiment-repo`#11.\n\n- **Constant-row sentence:** the new text says S̄ and the best degree benchmark \"do no better than a constant\". The table gives a constant of −0.239, S̄ at −0.216 and p(1−p) at −0.257. I asked for \"within 0.03 of a constant\", because I computed no interval for these differences.\n- **Abstract and intro:** \"matches the measured bias within Monte Carlo error in 85% of cells\" reads as an exact match in 85% of cells. What I computed is that the prediction lies inside the 95% Monte Carlo interval in 85.1% of 1224 cells (86.7% with finite-n centring). I asked for that wording.\n\nBlock H (mechanism g) finished. Block C shards, two HT shards and one GNN cell are running. The other GNN cells and HT shards are still queued. Nothing is aggregated until block C and the rest finish; I'll deliver the confirmatory results, baselines and the `REPRODUCE.md` update then."}}, {"id": "dd362db6-7c0f-5ec7-a4df-4c7b932ee264", "at": 1795654928.505198, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117814, "layer": "worker", "category": "usage", "kind": "session.usage", "role": "experiment-repo", "actor": "experiment-repo", "execution_id": "2e704c5754bd87da88c3584dd7ff4ca7", "trust": "agent-reported", "outcome": null, "label": "usage", "repository": null, "flags": [], "causes": [], "summary": "context usage"}, {"id": "9b964beb-2000-5118-97de-8a2b83764539", "at": 1795654928.513583, "clock": "host", "stream": "runner", "sequence": 117815, "layer": "worker", "category": "message", "kind": "session.res